PAIDAR.AI DECISION PACKET EXAMPLE (FILLED)
Project: AI-Assisted Student Services Intake

Section 1: Decision Context
- Decision title: Deploy AI intake copilot for advising tickets
- Decision owner: VP Student Success
- Date needed: 2026-06-15
- Trigger event: Backlog grew 42% over two terms
- Business objective: Reduce response time by 35% and improve first-contact resolution

Section 2: Problem Statement
- Current state: Advisors manually triage all inbound requests using email and spreadsheets
- Risk if unchanged: Delay in student support and lower retention outcomes
- Why now: Summer planning window enables policy updates and pilot rollout

Section 3: Options
Option A: Keep current workflow and hire two advisors
- Cost estimate: High recurring
- Time to value: Medium
- Risk level: Medium

Option B: Deploy AI copilot with supervised triage
- Cost estimate: Medium
- Time to value: Fast
- Risk level: Medium-Low

Option C: Full automation with no human review
- Cost estimate: Medium
- Time to value: Fast
- Risk level: High

Section 4: Evaluation Criteria
- Strategic alignment (25%): Option B highest
- Operational feasibility (20%): Option B highest
- Budget fit (20%): Option B highest
- Governance and compliance (20%): Option B acceptable with controls
- Adoption readiness (15%): Option B highest

Section 5: Recommended Path
- Selected option: Option B
- Why this option: Best balance of speed, governance, and measurable gains
- Dependencies: Policy updates, advisor training, CRM integration
- Fallback plan: Revert to manual triage queue for flagged intents

Section 6: Execution Plan (30/60/90)
- 30 days: Assessment, prompt/testing baseline, policy review
- 60 days: Pilot in two departments, weekly quality checks
- 90 days: Expand to all advising channels with executive dashboard

Section 7: Approval
- Executive sponsor: VP Student Success
- Functional leads: Advising Director, IT Director, Compliance Officer
- Decision date: 2026-05-20
